  "body": "If synapse is configured to interface with an external auth provider (such as LDAP), there is no mechanism for that external system to feed back to synapse if a user's credentials have been locked/revoked/etc. Synapse's `access_tokens` stay valid forever.\r\n\r\nA related question: if a user's password is changed in the external system, should we require all matrix clients to log in again, as we would with a local password change? If so, how should this be implemented?\r\n",
